IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `snap-core`
IMPORT `snap3-logic`

-- SECTION 2016, ISSUANCE AND USE OF PROGRAM BENEFITS (7 U.S.C. 2016), subsections (a) to (g): lines 913-975 of usc07-ch51.txt.
-- Subsection (h) is in snap3-s2016-h.l4, subsections (i) to (k) in snap3-s2016-i-to-k.l4.
-- Layer 1: the law, objectively. A function answers MAYBE BOOLEAN (or MAYBE NUMBER, MAYBE DATE) with: JUST TRUE = the text says yes;
-- JUST FALSE = the text says no in its own words; NOTHING = the text does not say. Money is a NUMBER of dollars.
-- The Secretary's judgments ("determines", "as determined by the Secretary") are conditional inputs, never guessed.
-- A function named "... has done ..." answers JUST TRUE if the act was done and NOTHING if not, because the text states no time by which a duty without a deadline must be done.
-- Source is a converter's plain-text rendering, not the official text.

-- THE DATE OF ENACTMENT of the Food, Conservation, and Energy Act of 2008, which subsection (f)(3) counts from.
-- The source credit at line 1199 lists two Public Laws for the 2008 amendments: 110-234 (22 May 2008) and 110-246 (18 June 2008). The module takes 18 June 2008 (NOTES.md, fork F-2016-1).
-- src:1199 | Pub. L. 110–246, § 4(a), title IV, §§ 4001(b), 4002(a)(4), 4113–4115(a), June 18, 2008
@ref s 2016(f)(3) the date of enactment of the Food, Conservation, and Energy Act of 2008 (src:1199)
`s 2016(f)(3) the date of enactment of the Food, Conservation, and Energy Act of 2008` MEANS Date 18 6 2008

-- THE DATE EFFECTIVE for manual vouchers, from the text of (f)(4)(A).
-- src:950 | Effective beginning on February 7, 2014
@ref s 2016(f)(4)(A) the date from which the bar on manual vouchers takes effect (src:950)
`s 2016(f)(4)(A) the date from which the bar on manual vouchers takes effect` MEANS Date 7 2 2014

§ `s 2016 -- issuance and use of program benefits`

§§ `s 2016(a) in general`

-- src:914 | (a) In general
-- src:915 | Except as provided in subsection (i), EBT cards shall be issued only to households which have been duly certified as eligible to participate in the supplemental nutrition assistance program.
@ref s 2016(a) EBT cards are issued only to households duly certified as eligible (src:914-915)
-- In plain words: an EBT card may be issued only to a household that has been duly certified as eligible; subsection (i) is the exception. The text sets a limit and does not itself require a card to go to every certified household.
GIVEN `s 2020(e) the household has been duly certified as eligible to participate in the supplemental nutrition assistance program` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the card is issued under subsection (i)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2016(a) an EBT card may be issued to the household` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the card is issued under subsection (i)` THEN
            -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "Except as provided in subsection (i)" and subsection (i) is encoded in snap3-s2016-i-to-k.l4
            NOTHING
        IF `s 2020(e) the household has been duly certified as eligible to participate in the supplemental nutrition assistance program` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "EBT cards shall be issued only to households which have been duly certified as eligible to participate in the supplemental nutrition assistance program"
            JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "only to households which have been duly certified"
            -- note (a limit that says whom the card may not go to; it does not say that a certified household must get one)
            NOTHING

§§ `s 2016(b) use`

-- src:917 | Benefits issued to eligible households shall be used by them only to purchase food from retail food stores which have been approved for participation in the supplemental nutrition assistance program at prices prevailing in such stores
@ref s 2016(b) benefits are used only to purchase food from approved retail food stores at prevailing prices (src:917)
-- In plain words: a household uses its benefits only to buy food, from a retail food store approved for the program, at the prices the store has for everyone.
-- The text both commands the use and limits it, so a use that meets all three conditions is the text's yes (NOTES.md, Marginal readings).
GIVEN `s 2012(g) the thing bought is food` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the household buys it from a retail food store which has been approved for participation in the supplemental nutrition assistance program` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the price is the price prevailing in such store` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2016(b) the household may use the benefits for the purchase` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 2012(g) the thing bought is food` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall be used by them only to purchase food"
            JUST FALSE
        IF `the household buys it from a retail food store which has been approved for participation in the supplemental nutrition assistance program` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "only to purchase food from retail food stores which have been approved for participation in the supplemental nutrition assistance program"
            JUST FALSE
        IF NOT `the price is the price prevailing in such store` THEN
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "at prices prevailing in such stores"
            JUST FALSE
        IF `s 2012(g) the thing bought is food` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `the household buys it from a retail food store which has been approved for participation in the supplemental nutrition assistance program` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the thing bought is food, and whether the store is approved, are answered elsewhere and were not supplied
            NOTHING

-- src:917 | Provided, That nothing in this chapter shall be construed as authorizing the Secretary to specify the prices at which food may be sold by wholesale food concerns or retail food stores.
@ref s 2016(b) nothing in the chapter authorizes the Secretary to specify the prices at which food may be sold (src:917)
-- In plain words: the chapter gives the Secretary no power to set the prices wholesale food concerns or retail food stores charge.
GIVEN `the Secretary would be specifying the prices at which food may be sold by wholesale food concerns or retail food stores` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2016(b) this chapter authorizes the Secretary to specify the prices` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the Secretary would be specifying the prices at which food may be sold by wholesale food concerns or retail food stores` THEN
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "nothing in this chapter shall be construed as authorizing the Secretary to specify the prices at which food may be sold by wholesale food concerns or retail food stores"
            JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the prices at which food may be sold by wholesale food concerns or retail food stores"
            NOTHING

§§ `s 2016(c) design`

-- src:918 | (c) Design
-- src:919 | (1) In general
-- src:920 | EBT cards issued to eligible households shall be simple in design and shall include only such words or illustrations as are required to explain their purpose.
@ref s 2016(c)(1) an EBT card is simple in design and carries only the words or illustrations needed to explain its purpose (src:918-920)
-- In plain words: the face of an EBT card issued to an eligible household is simple and shows only the words or pictures needed to explain what the card is for.
GIVEN `the card is simple in design` IS A BOOLEAN
      `every word and illustration on the card is required to explain its purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2016(c)(1) the EBT card is as the paragraph requires` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the card is simple in design` AND `every word and illustration on the card is required to explain its purpose` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall be simple in design and shall include only such words or illustrations as are required to explain their purpose"
            JUST FALSE

-- src:921 | (2) Prohibition
-- src:922 | The name of any public official shall not appear on any EBT card.
@ref s 2016(c)(2) the name of a public official does not appear on an EBT card (src:921-922)
GIVEN `the name of a public official appears on the EBT card` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2016(c)(2) the EBT card may bear the name of the public official` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the name of a public official appears on the EBT card` THEN
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The name of any public official shall not appear on any EBT card."
            JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The name of any public official"
            NOTHING

§§ `s 2016(e) State issuance liability`

-- src:925 | (e) State issuance liability
-- src:926 | Notwithstanding any other provision of this chapter, the State agency shall be strictly liable to the Secretary for any financial losses involved in the acceptance, storage and issuance of benefits, except that in the case of losses resulting from the issuance and replacement of authorizations for benefits which are sent through the mail, the State agency shall be liable to the Secretary to the extent prescribed in the regulations promulgated by the Secretary.
@ref s 2016(e) the State agency is strictly liable to the Secretary for financial losses in the acceptance, storage and issuance of benefits (src:925-926)
-- In plain words: a State agency bears the whole of any financial loss in accepting, storing or issuing benefits; the one exception is a loss from issuing or replacing authorizations that are sent through the mail, for which it is liable to the extent the Secretary's regulations prescribe.
GIVEN `the loss is a financial loss involved in the acceptance, storage and issuance of benefits` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the loss results from the issuance and replacement of authorizations for benefits which are sent through the mail` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2016(e) the State agency is strictly liable to the Secretary for the loss` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the loss is a financial loss involved in the acceptance, storage and issuance of benefits` THEN
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any financial losses involved in the acceptance, storage and issuance of benefits"
            NOTHING
        IF `the loss results from the issuance and replacement of authorizations for benefits which are sent through the mail` THEN
            -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "the State agency shall be liable to the Secretary to the extent prescribed in the regulations promulgated by the Secretary"
            NOTHING
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:925 | (e) State issuance liability
-- src:926 | Notwithstanding any other provision of this chapter, the State agency shall be strictly liable to the Secretary for any financial losses involved in the acceptance, storage and issuance of benefits, except that in the case of losses resulting from the issuance and replacement of authorizations for benefits which are sent through the mail, the State agency shall be liable to the Secretary to the extent prescribed in the regulations promulgated by the Secretary.
@ref s 2016(e) the amount of the loss for which the State agency is liable (src:925-926)
-- For a mailed authorization the text gives no figure: the share is "the extent prescribed in the regulations", an input (the dollars of the loss for which the regulations make the State agency liable).
GIVEN `the loss is a financial loss involved in the acceptance, storage and issuance of benefits` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the loss results from the issuance and replacement of authorizations for benefits which are sent through the mail` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount of the loss in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount of the loss in dollars for which the regulations make the State agency liable` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 2016(e) the amount of the loss for which the State agency is liable to the Secretary` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the loss is a financial loss involved in the acceptance, storage and issuance of benefits` THEN
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any financial losses involved in the acceptance, storage and issuance of benefits"
            NOTHING
        IF `the loss results from the issuance and replacement of authorizations for benefits which are sent through the mail` THEN
            -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "to the extent prescribed in the regulations promulgated by the Secretary"
            `the amount of the loss in dollars for which the regulations make the State agency liable`
        OTHERWISE JUST `the amount of the loss in dollars`

§§ `s 2016(f) alternative benefit delivery`

-- src:927 | (f) Alternative benefit delivery
-- src:928 | (1) In general
-- src:929 | If the Secretary determines, in consultation with the Inspector General of the Department of Agriculture, that it would improve the integrity of the supplemental nutrition assistance program, the Secretary shall require a State agency to issue or deliver benefits using alternative methods.
@ref s 2016(f)(1) the Secretary requires a State agency to use alternative methods of issue or delivery (src:927-929)
-- In plain words: if the Secretary determines, in consultation with the Inspector General, that alternative methods would improve the integrity of the program, the Secretary must require a State agency to use them.
GIVEN `the Secretary determines, in consultation with the Inspector General of the Department of Agriculture, that it would improve the integrity of the supplemental nutrition assistance program` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2016(f)(1) the Secretary must require a State agency to issue or deliver benefits using alternative methods` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the Secretary determines, in consultation with the Inspector General of the Department of Agriculture, that it would improve the integrity of the supplemental nutrition assistance program`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
        WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN JUST FALSE THEN
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the Secretary determines, in consultation with the Inspector General of the Department of Agriculture, that it would improve the integrity of the supplemental nutrition assistance program"
            -- note (a failed "if"; see NOTES.md, Marginal readings)
            JUST FALSE

-- src:930 | (2) Imposition of costs
-- src:931 | (A) In general
-- src:932 | Except as provided in subparagraph (B), the Secretary shall require participating retail food stores (including restaurants participating in a State option restaurant program intended to serve the elderly, disabled, and homeless) to pay 100 percent of the costs of acquiring, and arrange for the implementation of, electronic benefit transfer point-of-sale equipment and supplies, including related services.
@ref s 2016(f)(2)(A) the Secretary requires participating retail food stores to pay all the costs of EBT point-of-sale equipment (src:930-932)
-- In plain words: except for stores the Secretary exempts under subparagraph (B), participating retail food stores (restaurants in a State option restaurant program included) pay 100 percent of the cost of acquiring EBT point-of-sale equipment, supplies and related services, and the arrangement for putting it in place.
GIVEN `the store is a participating retail food store (including a restaurant participating in a State option restaurant program intended to serve the elderly, disabled, and homeless)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Secretary has exempted the store under subparagraph (B)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 2016(f)(2)(A) the percent of the costs the Secretary must require the store to pay` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the store is a participating retail food store (including a restaurant participating in a State option restaurant program intended to serve the elderly, disabled, and homeless)` THEN
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "participating retail food stores (including restaurants participating in a State option restaurant program intended to serve the elderly, disabled, and homeless)"
            NOTHING
        IF `the Secretary has exempted the store under subparagraph (B)` THEN
            -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text says the store is outside subparagraph (A) and names no other share for it
            NOTHING
        OTHERWISE JUST 100

-- src:933 | (B) Exemptions
-- src:934 | The Secretary may exempt from subparagraph (A)—
-- src:935 | (i) farmers’ markets and other direct-to-consumer markets, military commissaries, nonprofit food buying cooperatives, and establishments, organizations, programs, or group living arrangements described in paragraphs (5), (7), and (8) of section 2012(k) of this title; and
-- src:936 | (ii) establishments described in paragraphs (3), (4), and (9) of section 2012(k) of this title, other than restaurants participating in a State option restaurant program.
@ref s 2016(f)(2)(B) the Secretary may exempt a store from subparagraph (A) (src:933-936)
-- In plain words: the Secretary may exempt (i) farmers' markets and other direct-to-consumer markets, military commissaries, nonprofit food buying cooperatives, and the establishments in paragraphs (5), (7) and (8) of section 2012(k); and
-- (ii) the establishments in paragraphs (3), (4) and (9) of section 2012(k), other than restaurants in a State option restaurant program.
GIVEN `the store is a farmers' market or other direct-to-consumer market` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the store is a military commissary` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the store is a nonprofit food buying cooperative` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 2012(k) the establishment is one described in paragraphs (5), (7) and (8) of section 2012(k)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 2012(k) the establishment is one described in paragraphs (3), (4) and (9) of section 2012(k)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the store is a restaurant participating in a State option restaurant program` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2016(f)(2)(B) the Secretary may exempt the store from subparagraph (A)` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the store is a farmers' market or other direct-to-consumer market` OR `the store is a military commissary` OR `the store is a nonprofit food buying cooperative` OR `s 2012(k) the establishment is one described in paragraphs (5), (7) and (8) of section 2012(k)` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `s 2012(k) the establishment is one described in paragraphs (3), (4) and (9) of section 2012(k)` AND (NOT `the store is a restaurant participating in a State option restaurant program`) THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `s 2012(k) the establishment is one described in paragraphs (3), (4) and (9) of section 2012(k)` THEN
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "establishments described in paragraphs (3), (4), and (9) of section 2012(k) of this title, other than restaurants participating in a State option restaurant program"
            JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the exemption power is listed for the stores and establishments named in clauses (i) and (ii); the text does not close the list with "only"
            NOTHING

-- src:937 | (C) Interchange fees
-- src:938 | Nothing in this paragraph permits the charging of fees relating to the redemption of supplemental nutrition assistance program benefits, in accordance with subsection (h)(13).
@ref s 2016(f)(2)(C) paragraph (2) does not permit fees for redeeming benefits (src:937-938)
GIVEN `the fee relates to the redemption of supplemental nutrition assistance program benefits` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2016(f)(2)(C) paragraph (2) permits the charging of the fee` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the fee relates to the redemption of supplemental nutrition assistance program benefits` THEN
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Nothing in this paragraph permits the charging of fees relating to the redemption of supplemental nutrition assistance program benefits"
            JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "fees relating to the redemption of supplemental nutrition assistance program benefits"
            NOTHING

-- src:939 | (3) Devaluation and termination of issuance of paper coupons
-- src:940 | (A) Coupon issuance
-- src:941 | Effective on the date of enactment of the Food, Conservation, and Energy Act of 2008, no State shall issue any coupon, stamp, certificate, or authorization card to a household that receives supplemental nutrition assistance under this chapter.
@ref s 2016(f)(3)(A) no State issues coupons, stamps, certificates or authorization cards to a household (src:939-941)
-- In plain words: from the date of enactment of the 2008 Act no State may issue a coupon, stamp, certificate or authorization card to a household that receives SNAP.
GIVEN `the date of issue` IS A DATE
      `the thing issued is a coupon, stamp, certificate, or authorization card` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2016(f)(3)(A) a State may issue the thing to a household that receives supplemental nutrition assistance` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the thing issued is a coupon, stamp, certificate, or authorization card` THEN
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any coupon, stamp, certificate, or authorization card"
            NOTHING
        IF Day `the date of issue` LESS THAN Day `s 2016(f)(3) the date of enactment of the Food, Conservation, and Energy Act of 2008` THEN
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Effective on the date of enactment of the Food, Conservation, and Energy Act of 2008"
            NOTHING
        OTHERWISE
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "no State shall issue any coupon, stamp, certificate, or authorization card to a household that receives supplemental nutrition assistance under this chapter"
            JUST FALSE

-- src:942 | (B) EBT cards
-- src:943 | Effective beginning on the date that is 1 year after the date of enactment of the Food, Conservation, and Energy Act of 2008, only an EBT card issued under subsection (i) shall be eligible for exchange at any retail food store.
@ref s 2016(f)(3)(B) one year after enactment only an EBT card issued under subsection (i) is eligible for exchange at a retail food store (src:942-943)
-- In plain words: from one year after enactment only an EBT card issued under subsection (i) can be exchanged at any retail food store. As rendered, the text says subsection (i), the State option for certain individuals; NOTES.md, fork F-2016-2 and finding 1.
GIVEN `the date of the exchange` IS A DATE
      `the EBT card was issued under subsection (i)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2016(f)(3)(B) the card is eligible for exchange at a retail food store` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF Day `the date of the exchange` LESS THAN Day (`add years` `s 2016(f)(3) the date of enactment of the Food, Conservation, and Energy Act of 2008` 1) THEN
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Effective beginning on the date that is 1 year after the date of enactment of the Food, Conservation, and Energy Act of 2008"
            NOTHING
        IF NOT `the EBT card was issued under subsection (i)` THEN
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "only an EBT card issued under subsection (i) shall be eligible for exchange at any retail food store"
            JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "only an EBT card issued under subsection (i)"
            -- note (a necessary condition: the text does not say that every such card is eligible)
            NOTHING

-- src:944 | (C) De-obligation of coupons
-- src:945 | Coupons not redeemed during the 1-year period beginning on the date of enactment of the Food, Conservation, and Energy Act of 2008 shall—
-- src:946 | (i) no longer be an obligation of the Federal Government; and
-- src:947 | (ii) not be redeemable.
@ref s 2016(f)(3)(C) coupons not redeemed during the year after enactment are no longer an obligation of the Federal Government and are not redeemable (src:944-947)
-- In plain words: a coupon not redeemed in the one-year period that begins on the date of enactment stops being an obligation of the Government and can no longer be redeemed. The period runs from the date of enactment up to, not including, the same date a year later.
GIVEN `the date on which the question is asked` IS A DATE
      `the coupon was redeemed during the 1-year period beginning on the date of enactment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2016(f)(3)(C) the coupon is still an obligation of the Federal Government` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the coupon was redeemed during the 1-year period beginning on the date of enactment` THEN
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Coupons not redeemed during the 1-year period beginning on the date of enactment"
            NOTHING
        IF Day `the date on which the question is asked` LESS THAN Day (`add years` `s 2016(f)(3) the date of enactment of the Food, Conservation, and Energy Act of 2008` 1) THEN
            -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the period has not ended, so the text does not yet say the coupon is no longer an obligation
            NOTHING
        OTHERWISE
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall— (i) no longer be an obligation of the Federal Government"
            JUST FALSE

-- src:944 | (C) De-obligation of coupons
-- src:945 | Coupons not redeemed during the 1-year period beginning on the date of enactment of the Food, Conservation, and Energy Act of 2008 shall—
-- src:946 | (i) no longer be an obligation of the Federal Government; and
-- src:947 | (ii) not be redeemable.
@ref s 2016(f)(3)(C) the coupon is redeemable (src:944-947)
GIVEN `the date on which the question is asked` IS A DATE
      `the coupon was redeemed during the 1-year period beginning on the date of enactment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2016(f)(3)(C) the coupon is redeemable` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the coupon was redeemed during the 1-year period beginning on the date of enactment` THEN
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Coupons not redeemed during the 1-year period beginning on the date of enactment"
            NOTHING
        IF Day `the date on which the question is asked` LESS THAN Day (`add years` `s 2016(f)(3) the date of enactment of the Food, Conservation, and Energy Act of 2008` 1) THEN
            -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the period has not ended, so the text does not yet say the coupon is not redeemable
            NOTHING
        OTHERWISE
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(ii) not be redeemable"
            JUST FALSE

-- src:948 | (4) Termination of manual vouchers
-- src:949 | (A) In general
-- src:950 | Effective beginning on February 7, 2014, except as provided in subparagraph (B), no State shall issue manual vouchers to a household that receives supplemental nutrition assistance under this chapter or allow retail food stores to accept manual vouchers as payment, unless the Secretary determines that the manual vouchers are necessary, such as in the event of an electronic benefit transfer system failure or a disaster situation.
@ref s 2016(f)(4)(A) from 7 February 2014 no State issues manual vouchers or lets retail food stores accept them (src:948-950)
-- In plain words: from 7 February 2014 no State may issue a manual voucher to a SNAP household or allow a retail food store to accept one as payment, unless the Secretary determines manual vouchers are necessary, for example in an EBT failure or a disaster. The opening "except as provided in subparagraph (B)" is a separate power of the Secretary and is asked of `s 2016(f)(4)(B) the Secretary may exempt the category of retail food stores or the individual retail food store from subparagraph (A)`; this function answers subparagraph (A) alone.
GIVEN `the date of issue or acceptance` IS A DATE
      `the Secretary determines that the manual vouchers are necessary` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2016(f)(4)(A) a State may issue manual vouchers to a household or allow retail food stores to accept them` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF Day `the date of issue or acceptance` LESS THAN Day `s 2016(f)(4)(A) the date from which the bar on manual vouchers takes effect` THEN
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Effective beginning on February 7, 2014"
            NOTHING
        IF `the Secretary determines that the manual vouchers are necessary` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "unless the Secretary determines that the manual vouchers are necessary"
            -- note (the exception lifts the bar and the text does not itself give permission)
            NOTHING
        IF `the Secretary determines that the manual vouchers are necessary` EQUALS NOTHING THEN
            -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the Secretary has determined that manual vouchers are necessary was not supplied
            NOTHING
        OTHERWISE
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "no State shall issue manual vouchers to a household that receives supplemental nutrition assistance under this chapter or allow retail food stores to accept manual vouchers as payment"
            JUST FALSE

-- src:951 | (B) Exemptions
-- src:952 | The Secretary may exempt categories of retail food stores or individual retail food stores from subparagraph (A) based on criteria established by the Secretary.
@ref s 2016(f)(4)(B) the Secretary may exempt categories of retail food stores or individual stores from subparagraph (A) (src:951-952)
GIVEN `the exemption is based on criteria established by the Secretary` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2016(f)(4)(B) the Secretary may exempt the category of retail food stores or the individual retail food store from subparagraph (A)` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the exemption is based on criteria established by the Secretary`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
        WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN JUST FALSE THEN
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "based on criteria established by the Secretary"
            -- note (a failed condition; see NOTES.md, Marginal readings)
            JUST FALSE

-- src:953 | (5) Unique identification number required
-- src:954 | (A) In general
-- src:955 | To enhance the anti-fraud protections of the program, the Secretary shall require all parties providing electronic benefit transfer services to provide for and maintain unique terminal identification number information through the supplemental nutrition assistance program electronic benefit transfer transaction routing system.
@ref s 2016(f)(5)(A) the Secretary requires all parties providing EBT services to maintain unique terminal identification number information (src:953-955)
GIVEN `the Secretary has required all parties providing electronic benefit transfer services to provide for and maintain unique terminal identification number information through the supplemental nutrition assistance program electronic benefit transfer transaction routing system` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2016(f)(5)(A) the Secretary has done what the subparagraph requires` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the Secretary has required all parties providing electronic benefit transfer services to provide for and maintain unique terminal identification number information through the supplemental nutrition assistance program electronic benefit transfer transaction routing system` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text states no time by which the Secretary must require it
            NOTHING

-- src:961 | (C) Operation of individual point of sale device by farmers’ markets and direct marketing farmers
-- src:962 | A farmers’ market or direct marketing farmer that is exempt under paragraph (2)(B)(i) shall be allowed to operate an individual electronic benefit transfer point of sale device at more than 1 location under the same supplemental nutrition assistance program authorization, if—
-- src:963 | (i) the farmers’ market or direct marketing farmer provides to the Secretary information on location and hours of operation at each location; and
-- src:964 | (ii)
-- src:965 | (I) the point of sale device used by the farmers’ market or direct marketing farmer is capable of providing location information of the device through the electronic benefit transfer system; or
-- src:966 | (II) if the Secretary determines that the technology is not available for a point of sale device to meet the requirement under subclause (I), the farmers’ market or direct marketing farmer provides to the Secretary any other information, as determined by the Secretary, necessary to ensure the integrity of transactions processed using the point of sale device.
@ref s 2016(f)(5)(C) a farmers' market or direct marketing farmer exempt under paragraph (2)(B)(i) may operate one point-of-sale device at more than 1 location (src:961-966)
-- In plain words: an exempt farmers' market or direct marketing farmer is allowed to run one EBT point-of-sale device at several locations under the same authorization, if it tells the Secretary where and when it operates at each,
-- and either the device reports its own location through the EBT system or, where the Secretary finds that technology is not available, the farmer gives the Secretary the other information the Secretary requires to protect the integrity of transactions.
GIVEN `the farmers' market or direct marketing farmer is exempt under paragraph (2)(B)(i)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it provides to the Secretary information on location and hours of operation at each location` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the device is capable of providing location information of the device through the electronic benefit transfer system` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Secretary determines that the technology is not available for a point of sale device to meet the requirement under subclause (I)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `it provides to the Secretary any other information, as determined by the Secretary, necessary to ensure the integrity of transactions processed using the point of sale device` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2016(f)(5)(C) the farmers' market or direct marketing farmer shall be allowed to operate the device at more than 1 location under the same authorization` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the farmers' market or direct marketing farmer is exempt under paragraph (2)(B)(i)` THEN
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A farmers' market or direct marketing farmer that is exempt under paragraph (2)(B)(i)"
            NOTHING
        IF NOT `it provides to the Secretary information on location and hours of operation at each location` THEN
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if— (i) the farmers' market or direct marketing farmer provides to the Secretary information on location and hours of operation at each location"
            -- note (a failed "if"; see NOTES.md, Marginal readings)
            JUST FALSE
        IF `the device is capable of providing location information of the device through the electronic benefit transfer system` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the Secretary determines that the technology is not available for a point of sale device to meet the requirement under subclause (I)` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `it provides to the Secretary any other information, as determined by the Secretary, necessary to ensure the integrity of transactions processed using the point of sale device` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the Secretary determines that the technology is not available for a point of sale device to meet the requirement under subclause (I)` EQUALS NOTHING THEN
            -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the Secretary has determined the technology is not available was not supplied
            NOTHING
        OTHERWISE
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(ii) (I) the point of sale device used by the farmers’ market or direct marketing farmer is capable of providing location information of the device through the electronic benefit transfer system; or (II) if the Secretary determines that the technology is not available"
            -- note (a failed "if"; see NOTES.md, Marginal readings)
            JUST FALSE

§§ `s 2016(g) staggered issuance procedures`

-- src:968 | (1) The State agency may establish a procedure for staggering the issuance of benefits to eligible households throughout the month.
@ref s 2016(g)(1) the State agency may establish a procedure for staggering issuance (src:968)
GIVEN `the State agency establishes a procedure for staggering the issuance of benefits to eligible households throughout the month` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2016(g)(1) the State agency may establish a procedure for staggering the issuance of benefits` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the State agency establishes a procedure for staggering the issuance of benefits to eligible households throughout the month` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The State agency may establish a procedure for staggering the issuance of benefits to eligible households throughout the month."
            NOTHING

-- src:968 | Upon the request of the tribal organization that exercises governmental jurisdiction over the reservation, the State agency shall stagger the issuance of benefits for eligible households located on reservations for at least 15 days of a month.
@ref s 2016(g)(1) on a tribal organization's request the State agency staggers issuance on reservations for at least 15 days (src:968)
-- In plain words: when the tribal organization that governs the reservation asks, the State agency must stagger issuance to eligible households on the reservation over at least 15 days of the month.
GIVEN `the tribal organization that exercises governmental jurisdiction over the reservation has made the request` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the households are eligible households located on the reservation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2016(g)(1) the State agency must stagger the issuance of benefits for the households` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the tribal organization that exercises governmental jurisdiction over the reservation has made the request` AND `the households are eligible households located on the reservation` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Upon the request of the tribal organization that exercises governmental jurisdiction over the reservation"
            -- note (the first sentence leaves staggering optional when there is no request)
            NOTHING

-- src:968 | the State agency shall stagger the issuance of benefits for eligible households located on reservations for at least 15 days of a month.
@ref s 2016(g)(1) the staggering on a reservation covers at least 15 days of a month (src:968)
GIVEN `the number of days of the month over which issuance is staggered` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2016(g)(1) the staggering for households on reservations meets the requirement` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the number of days of the month over which issuance is staggered` AT LEAST 15 THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "for at least 15 days of a month"
            JUST FALSE

-- src:969 | (2) Requirements.—
-- src:970 | (A) In general.—
-- src:971 | Any procedure established under paragraph (1) shall—
-- src:972 | (i) not reduce the allotment of any household for any period; and
-- src:973 | (ii) ensure that no household experiences an interval between issuances of more than 40 days.
@ref s 2016(g)(2)(A)(i) a staggering procedure does not reduce the allotment of any household for any period (src:969-973)
GIVEN `the amount by which the procedure reduces the allotment of the household for the period` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2016(g)(2)(A)(i) the procedure meets the requirement that it not reduce the allotment of any household` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the amount by which the procedure reduces the allotment of the household for the period` GREATER THAN 0 THEN
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Any procedure established under paragraph (1) shall— (i) not reduce the allotment of any household for any period"
            JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:969 | (2) Requirements.—
-- src:970 | (A) In general.—
-- src:971 | Any procedure established under paragraph (1) shall—
-- src:972 | (i) not reduce the allotment of any household for any period; and
-- src:973 | (ii) ensure that no household experiences an interval between issuances of more than 40 days.
@ref s 2016(g)(2)(A)(ii) a staggering procedure ensures no household has an interval of more than 40 days between issuances (src:969-973)
-- In plain words: under the procedure, no household waits more than 40 days between one issuance and the next. Forty days exactly is allowed.
GIVEN `the number of days between two issuances to the household` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2016(g)(2)(A)(ii) the interval between issuances meets the requirement` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the number of days between two issuances to the household` AT MOST 40 THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "ensure that no household experiences an interval between issuances of more than 40 days"
            JUST FALSE

-- src:974 | (B) Multiple issuances.—
-- src:975 | The procedure may include issuing benefits to a household in more than 1 issuance during a month only when a benefit correction is necessary.
@ref s 2016(g)(2)(B) the procedure may include more than one issuance in a month only when a benefit correction is necessary (src:974-975)
GIVEN `the number of issuances to the household in the month` IS A NUMBER
      `a benefit correction is necessary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2016(g)(2)(B) the procedure may include the issuances` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the number of issuances to the household in the month` AT MOST 1 THEN
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "issuing benefits to a household in more than 1 issuance during a month"
            NOTHING
        IF `a benefit correction is necessary` THEN
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "only when a benefit correction is necessary"
            -- note (a necessary condition: the text does not say that a correction makes every extra issuance permitted)
            NOTHING
        OTHERWISE
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The procedure may include issuing benefits to a household in more than 1 issuance during a month only when a benefit correction is necessary."
            JUST FALSE
